WEBVTT

1
00:00:29.875 --> 00:00:30.916
<b>Here, Lord Krishna explains</b>

2
00:00:30.916 --> 00:00:34.916
<b>the fundamental principle of Nishkama Karma </b>
<b>Yoga (the path of selfless action).</b>

3
00:00:34.916 --> 00:00:35.958
<b>He teaches:</b>

4
00:00:35.958 --> 00:00:41.791
<b>"Walk the path of Yoga by </b>
<b>fulfilling only your duties,</b>

5
00:00:41.791 --> 00:00:44.541
<b>letting go of all attachments. </b>

6
00:00:44.541 --> 00:00:48.666
<b>Maintain equanimity in</b>
<b>both success and failure.</b>

7
00:00:48.666 --> 00:00:52.333
<b>Such steadiness of mind is</b>
<b>what truly defines 'Yoga.'"</b>

8
00:00:57.208 --> 00:01:04.041
<b>When one completely renounces attachment </b>
<b>to outcomes and focuses solely on their actions,</b>

9
00:01:04.041 --> 00:01:06.875
<b>this is called Karma Yoga.</b>

10
00:01:06.875 --> 00:01:13.583
<b>Actions performed continuously in this manner </b>
<b>ultimately unite one with the Divine.</b>

11
00:01:13.583 --> 00:01:14.500
<b>Therefore,</b>

12
00:01:14.500 --> 00:01:17.958
<b>Arjuna must never abandon his duty.</b>

13
00:01:17.958 --> 00:01:21.791
<b>Actions performed without </b>
<b>expectation or attachment</b>

14
00:01:21.791 --> 00:01:25.166
<b>are capable of elevating one's</b>
<b>spiritual consciousness.</b>

15
00:01:25.166 --> 00:01:28.708
<b>If Arjuna must renounce something, </b>
<b>it should not be his actions,</b>

16
00:01:28.708 --> 00:01:32.208
<b>but rather the desire for their fruits.</b>

17
00:01:32.208 --> 00:01:35.916
<b>People hold various beliefs about Yoga.</b>

18
00:01:35.916 --> 00:01:39.458
<b>Some see it merely as physical exercise,</b>

19
00:01:39.458 --> 00:01:45.041
<b>while others interpret it as</b>
<b>deep concentration in any activity.</b>

20
00:01:45.041 --> 00:01:46.208
<b>However, here</b>

21
00:01:46.208 --> 00:01:50.458
<b>Lord Krishna reveals its true meaning.</b>
<b>Yoga</b>

22
00:01:50.458 --> 00:01:56.958
<b>emotional stability through life's joys and </b>
<b>sorrows, ups and downs, good times and bad </b>

23
00:01:56.958 --> 00:01:58.666
<b>this is true Yoga.</b>

24
00:01:58.666 --> 00:02:00.875
<b>"Equanimity is Yoga"</b>

25
00:02:00.875 --> 00:02:03.458
<b>Balance itself is Yoga.</b>

26
00:02:03.458 --> 00:02:10.291
<b>Such a Karma Yogi finds such profound </b>
<b>satisfaction in merely performing their duty</b>

27
00:02:10.291 --> 00:02:13.541
<b>that the thought of rewards </b>
<b>never even enters their mind!</b>

28
00:02:18.333 --> 00:02:21.875
<b>Life is not a short race,</b>

29
00:02:21.875 --> 00:02:28.666
<b>It is a long journey towards your destination.</b>

30
00:02:28.666 --> 00:02:30.250
<b>On this path,</b>

31
00:02:30.250 --> 00:02:33.291
<b>sometimes you'll slow down,</b>

32
00:02:33.291 --> 00:02:36.500
<b>sometimes quicken your pace,</b>

33
00:02:36.500 --> 00:02:39.333
<b>sometimes you'll lead,</b>

34
00:02:39.333 --> 00:02:43.333
<b>and sometimes others will move ahead.</b>

35
00:02:43.333 --> 00:02:46.791
<b>This journey will have many milestones</b>

36
00:02:46.791 --> 00:02:48.583
<b>some of success,</b>

37
00:02:48.583 --> 00:02:52.166
<b>some of failure.</b>

38
00:02:52.166 --> 00:02:53.125
<b>If you</b>

39
00:02:53.125 --> 00:02:56.916
<b>possess emotional stability,</b>

40
00:02:56.916 --> 00:03:06.041
<b>these milestones of success or</b>
<b>failure won't affect you adversely.</b>

41
00:03:06.041 --> 00:03:10.041
<b>Neither will failure dampen your spirit,</b>

42
00:03:10.041 --> 00:03:14.208
<b>nor will success make you arrogant.</b>

43
00:03:14.208 --> 00:03:15.666
<b>But</b>

44
00:03:15.666 --> 00:03:22.041
<b>if you tend toward emotional imbalance,</b>

45
00:03:22.041 --> 00:03:26.041
<b>this journey will become extremely painful,</b>

46
00:03:26.041 --> 00:03:34.500
<b>for you know well that life's very </b>
<b>nature is its ups and downs.</b>

47
00:03:34.500 --> 00:03:38.541
<b>In success, you'll feel sky-high;</b>

48
00:03:38.541 --> 00:03:40.333
<b>in failure,</b>

49
00:03:40.333 --> 00:03:44.583
<b>you'll feel buried in the dust.</b>

50
00:03:44.583 --> 00:03:46.416
<b>How meaningless</b>

51
00:03:46.416 --> 00:03:49.458
<b>it is to live in such constant flux.</b>

52
00:03:49.458 --> 00:03:51.041
<b>Therefore,</b>

53
00:03:51.041 --> 00:03:53.333
<b>a true Karma Yogi</b>

54
00:03:53.333 --> 00:03:57.458
<b>remains focused solely on their duty.</b>

55
00:03:57.458 --> 00:04:04.375
<b>Their attention stays fixed</b>
<b>on what they can control</b>

56
00:04:04.375 --> 00:04:07.583
<b>their actions.</b>

57
00:04:07.583 --> 00:04:18.291
<b>They neither rest on good results</b>
<b>nor sit defeated by poor ones.</b>

58
00:04:18.291 --> 00:04:23.958
<b>From good results, they learn what to continue;</b>

59
00:04:23.958 --> 00:04:31.083
<b>from poor results, they learn what to change.</b>

60
00:04:31.083 --> 00:04:33.708
<b>They learn from everything,</b>

61
00:04:33.708 --> 00:04:37.208
<b>but never stop.</b>

62
00:04:37.208 --> 00:04:40.708
<b>They keep moving forward.</b>

63
00:04:40.708 --> 00:04:42.541
<b>And soon,</b>

64
00:04:42.541 --> 00:04:46.791
<b>this very process of continuous</b>
<b>learning and progression</b>

65
00:04:46.791 --> 00:04:51.166
<b>becomes their source of profound satisfaction.</b>

66
00:04:51.166 --> 00:04:54.625
<b>The action itself becomes their reward.</b>

67
00:04:54.625 --> 00:05:01.625
<b>A true Karma Yogi finds joy </b>
<b>in the very act of doing.</b>

68
00:05:01.625 --> 00:05:03.125
<b>You tell me,</b>

69
00:05:03.125 --> 00:05:05.333
<b>in the work you're doing</b>

70
00:05:05.333 --> 00:05:09.625
<b>are you finding complete joy in it?</b>

71
00:05:09.625 --> 00:05:12.875
<b>Consider another thing</b>

72
00:05:12.875 --> 00:05:14.916
<b>during a long journey,</b>

73
00:05:14.916 --> 00:05:19.250
<b>where do you spend more time?</b>

74
00:05:19.250 --> 00:05:20.958
<b>Walking on the path,</b>

75
00:05:20.958 --> 00:05:21.958
<b>or</b>

76
00:05:21.958 --> 00:05:26.791
<b>stopping at milestones?</b>

77
00:05:26.791 --> 00:05:29.083
<b>Walking on the path,</b>

78
00:05:29.083 --> 00:05:30.916
<b>right?</b>

79
00:05:30.916 --> 00:05:33.375
<b>Now think</b>

80
00:05:33.375 --> 00:05:37.833
<b>if you must keep walking for long,</b>

81
00:05:37.833 --> 00:05:43.500
<b>isn't it logical to make that walking itself joyful?</b>

82
00:05:43.500 --> 00:05:47.500
<b>Make your source of contentment not the fleeting </b>
<b>milestones of success/failure, </b>

83
00:05:47.500 --> 00:05:54.500
<b>but the long road that leads there.</b>

84
00:05:54.500 --> 00:05:58.708
<b>Make your actions your source of joy.</b>

85
00:05:58.708 --> 00:06:00.750
<b>Become a Karma Yogi.</b>

86
00:06:05.458 --> 00:06:08.291
<b>In society and family,</b>

87
00:06:08.291 --> 00:06:11.875
<b>people hold many expectations of us.</b>

88
00:06:11.875 --> 00:06:18.250
<b>Often, we become troubled by the</b>
<b>weight of these expectations.</b>

89
00:06:18.250 --> 00:06:22.916
<b>When we fail to meet these expectations,</b>

90
00:06:22.916 --> 00:06:26.333
<b>we react in two ways:</b>

91
00:06:26.333 --> 00:06:30.291
<b>either we become crushed under </b>
<b>the weight of self-guilt,</b>

92
00:06:30.291 --> 00:06:31.166
<b>or</b>

93
00:06:31.166 --> 00:06:33.750
<b>we start finding fault in others,</b>

94
00:06:33.750 --> 00:06:37.166
<b>blaming life itself,</b>

95
00:06:37.166 --> 00:06:43.166
<b>feeling that what's happening to you isn't right.</b>

96
00:06:43.166 --> 00:06:44.958
<b>Think about it.</b>

97
00:06:44.958 --> 00:06:49.166
<b>Will such thinking change your life?</b>

98
00:06:49.166 --> 00:06:52.916
<b>Will it improve your situation?</b>

99
00:06:52.916 --> 00:06:54.583
<b>No, it won't.</b>

100
00:06:54.583 --> 00:07:01.250
<b>Try to understand this not just spiritually, </b>
<b>but logically as well.</b>

101
00:07:01.250 --> 00:07:06.291
<b>In the turbulence of family and social life,</b>

102
00:07:06.291 --> 00:07:12.833
<b>what's the better way to handle any situation?</b>

103
00:07:12.833 --> 00:07:15.958
<b>Becoming disturbed by it?</b>

104
00:07:15.958 --> 00:07:17.250
<b>Or</b>

105
00:07:17.250 --> 00:07:21.541
<b>understanding it calmly?</b>

106
00:07:21.541 --> 00:07:24.875
<b>A peaceful response is the right response.</b>

107
00:07:24.875 --> 00:07:32.666
<b>And for this, emotional stability is essential.</b>

108
00:07:32.666 --> 00:07:37.166
<b>If you remain emotionally stable,</b>

109
00:07:37.166 --> 00:07:40.208
<b>self-guilt won't torment you,</b>

110
00:07:40.208 --> 00:07:45.583
<b>nor will you blame others for your circumstances.</b>

111
00:07:45.583 --> 00:07:47.875
<b>You'll simply know that</b>

112
00:07:47.875 --> 00:07:51.333
<b>ups and downs are part of life,</b>

113
00:07:51.333 --> 00:07:54.916
<b>and if you continue peacefully,</b>

114
00:07:54.916 --> 00:08:02.166
<b>these social and family situations </b>
<b>will pass on their own.</b>

115
00:08:02.166 --> 00:08:07.000
<b>Know that everything rights itself in time.</b>

116
00:08:07.000 --> 00:08:10.750
<b>Do whatever you can from your end.</b>

117
00:08:10.750 --> 00:08:16.666
<b>Face any situation with emotional equilibrium.</b>

118
00:08:16.666 --> 00:08:22.416
<b>This is equivalent to yoga </b>
<b>in social and family settings.</b>

119
00:08:27.250 --> 00:08:28.500
<b>Perhaps</b>

120
00:08:28.500 --> 00:08:32.041
<b>we face success and failure</b>

121
00:08:32.041 --> 00:08:40.791
<b>more in professional life </b>
<b>than in personal or family life.</b>

122
00:08:40.791 --> 00:08:43.500
<b>Is being successful or unsuccessful</b>

123
00:08:43.500 --> 00:08:47.750
<b>completely under your control?</b>

124
00:08:47.750 --> 00:08:49.458
<b>Think on it!</b>

125
00:08:49.458 --> 00:08:50.750
<b>No, right?</b>

126
00:08:50.750 --> 00:08:56.083
<b>But one thing is certainly in your control,</b>

127
00:08:56.083 --> 00:08:57.750
<b>and that's</b>

128
00:08:57.750 --> 00:09:02.791
<b>your response to any outcome.</b>

129
00:09:02.791 --> 00:09:10.458
<b>Controlling your response, and for</b>
<b>that controlling your emotions,</b>

130
00:09:10.458 --> 00:09:14.583
<b>is extremely crucial in professional life.</b>

131
00:09:14.583 --> 00:09:20.916
<b>If you maintain control over your emotions, </b>
<b>don't get easily disturbed,</b>

132
00:09:20.916 --> 00:09:26.416
<b>then even in failure you'll calmly see</b>

133
00:09:26.416 --> 00:09:30.500
<b>what opportunities exist to improve your work.</b>

134
00:09:30.500 --> 00:09:35.875
<b>And when you improve your work </b>
<b>using these opportunities,</b>

135
00:09:35.875 --> 00:09:39.416
<b>it will help you moving forward.</b>

136
00:09:39.416 --> 00:09:42.666
<b>Continuously improving your work,</b>

137
00:09:42.666 --> 00:09:44.583
<b>raising its standard</b>

138
00:09:44.583 --> 00:09:50.291
<b>this is the shadow of success in professional life.</b>

139
00:09:50.291 --> 00:09:53.708
<b>But there's another satisfying aspect here,</b>

140
00:09:53.708 --> 00:09:55.250
<b>and that is,</b>

141
00:09:55.250 --> 00:09:59.916
<b>after continuously improving </b>
<b>your work for some time,</b>

142
00:09:59.916 --> 00:10:04.958
<b>you'll start finding joy in this very process.</b>

143
00:10:04.958 --> 00:10:07.125
<b>Doing your work well,</b>

144
00:10:07.125 --> 00:10:09.083
<b>keeping on improving it</b>

145
00:10:09.083 --> 00:10:13.250
<b>you'll start finding contentment in this itself.</b>

146
00:10:13.250 --> 00:10:16.708
<b>Good results will become merely indicators</b>

147
00:10:16.708 --> 00:10:19.333
<b>that you're on the right path,</b>

148
00:10:19.333 --> 00:10:25.208
<b>while adverse results will become</b>
<b>opportunities to learn something new. </b>

149
00:10:25.208 --> 00:10:29.666
<b>You'll view both outcomes </b>
<b>with equal satisfaction.</b>

150
00:10:29.666 --> 00:10:33.083
<b>And thus, in professional life,</b>

151
00:10:33.083 --> 00:10:36.458
<b>you'll become a Karma Yogi.</b>

